   143	- **(R2) Smoothness.** θ = O(D^{2α−1}).
   144	- **(R3) Norm-product exponent.** θ = θ_coeff + (d − 1)ν with ν = 1/(4k). This holds for the box V ≈ √ℓ·S, whose
   145	  rational value is ‖g‖V/ℓ and whose algebraic value is ‖f‖V^d.
   146	
   147	For SNFS, θ_SNFS = 1/d + (d − 1)/(4k) + O(d log S/t): the randomisation floors of Theorem U's design (h ≥ 2ν, level,
   148	window) are absent because nothing is randomised.
   149	
   150	**Prop UF (universal one-level floor).** Suppose θ_coeff ≥ c·d^{−p} with c > 0 and p ≥ 0. Then α ≥ (1 + p)/(3p + 2)
   151	(and 1/2 for p = 0). By the Corollary of RES, every pair with a linear side has p ≤ 1, so **α ≥ 2/5 for every
   152	one-level design, special or not.**
