   489	## 7. Candidate card
   490	
   491	- **Mechanism.** SNFS fixed polynomials f_d = x^d − sr^j (degree chosen per node) inside the project's
   492	  Dixon-split + descent architecture. Randomness from w, kN, twists, root twists, several (d, j), special-q.
   493	- **Model.** [rec]/[nest] size model; Theorem U's supply framework.
   494	- **Result.**
   495	  - Size model: one-level 2/5 (universal, Prop UF), multi-level 1/3, rational-only 1/3 (Prop R2-S; GNFS: 2/5).
   496	  - Rigorous: the best α is 2/5 (Theorem U); constant ε_e^{2/5} for r^e ± 1 (Prop CY), o(1) along primorial e.
   497	- **Failure scope.**
   498	  - (O1) Fixed fields: HR/RS/PH/DI show that randomisation keeps the value set or costs height N^{1/d}.
   499	    RB: relativising supply proofs fail for any fixed family of N^{o(ν)} fields.
   500	  - (O2) Recognition (Prop REC): the split halves are not special. HECM or Theorem U recursion gives 2/5.
   501	- **Most promising open question.** A pointwise friable-values estimate for the Kummer forms a^d − cb^d on special-q
   502	  lattices at L-scale (Hypothesis RT), even only for the rational half a − b·r^j (prescribed-digit smooth numbers).

