   178	### 1.3 Multi-level descent in one field [model arithmetic, as [rec] §3.4]
   179	
   180	With d = D^δ, a level-j prime of log-size t^{β_j} has values of log-sizes t^{1−δ} (rational, ≈ log m) and t^{δ+β_j}
   181	(algebraic). These exponents are the same for GNFS and SNFS heights, because only the constants differ. So the level
   182	count ⌈(1 − 2α)/(3α − 1)⌉ (`sizemodel.multilevel_levels`) and the floor 1/3 (attained with O(log log N) levels at
   183	constant contraction) are unchanged. The obstruction there is nested's: algebraic children are field-bound ([nest]
   184	Lemma FB, Lemma OD).
   185	
   186	### 1.4 Prop R2-S: designs without algebraic children [proved (model arithmetic)]
   187	
   188	Nested's Prop R2 premises are (M1) (d + 1)log H_f + 2 log H_g ≳ t, (M2) typical sizes, (M3) random-integer
   189	smoothness, and (M4) split targets z₁ ≍ t^{1−α}(log t)^α. Under them, designs whose algebraic values are all B-smooth
   190	have α ≥ 2/5. Nested itself notes that (M1) is only a counting heuristic, and that small-height f breaks it.
   191	
   192	**Premise (M1-S).** For every degree 2 ≤ d ≤ D there is an irreducible pair with log H_f ≤ d log r + log|s| =
   193	O(d) and log H_g ≤ t/d + O(1) (the family f_d, m_d above; for 𝔈 every d works). (M2)–(M4) are kept, and each node
   194	may choose its own d.
   195	
   196	**Prop R2-S.**
   197	(i) For α > 1/3, a rational-only descent tree exists with a bounded number of levels, ⌈(1 − 2α)/(3α − 1)⌉.
   198	(ii) At α = 1/3 it exists with O(log log N) levels, whose targets contract by a constant factor.
   199	(iii) For α < 1/3 every node expands its targets, so no finite tree exists.
   200	So the floor is **1/3** instead of 2/5.
   201	
   202	*Derivation (model arithmetic).*
   203	- **Algebraic side.** A node with rational target q = e^z uses a reduced special-q box of radius e^{sΛ}√q in the field
   204	  of degree d. Its algebraic value has log-size d(z/2 + sΛ) + O(d). B-smoothness within budget needs this to be
   205	  ≤ φ_FΞ, so choose d(z) := ⌊φ_FΞ/(z/2 + sΛ)⌋.
   206	- **Rational cofactor.** Its log-size is t/d − z/2 + sΛ ≈ t(z/2 + sΛ)/(φ_FΞ). For it to be e^y-smooth within budget,
   207	  y ≥ (log-size)/(φ_RU), so y/z ≈ t(1/2 + sΛ/z)/(φ_Fφ_RΞU).
   208	- **Contraction.** Since ΞU ≍ t^{3α}(log t)^{1−3α}, the ratio is ≍ t^{1−3α}(log t)^{3α−1}. That is a polynomial
   209	  contraction for α > 1/3, a constant for α = 1/3 and an expansion for α < 1/3 (`sizemodel.r2s_contraction_exponent`).
   210	  For (iii), the reverse inequality d ≤ φ_FΞ/(z/2) forces a rational size ≥ tz/(2φ_FΞ), hence y/z → ∞ (codex
   211	  snfsrig_1 makes the same argument).
   212	- **At α = 1/3.** Write E = Λ_{1/3}, Q = t^{2/3}(log t)^{1/3}, D′ = Q/E, so t = D′Q.
   213	  - Parameters: B = e^{bE}, box radius e^{sE}√q, u_F = φ_FD′, u_R = φ_RD′, top targets z₁ = b₁Q.
