   329	### 2.5 Prop RB (relativisation barrier for fixed field families) [proved]
   330	
   331	**Setting.** A one-level design 𝔇 is given by Φ fixed pairs (f_i, g_i) (devices allowed) and the special-q targets
   332	ℓ ∈ J. Each target is searched in a box of ≤ W points of its lattice; [U] has W ≤ 400S². For a set 𝒮 ⊂ Z let
   333	γ_𝔇(𝒮) be the descendability density of [U] §1 computed with 𝒮 in place of the B-smooth integers 𝒮_B. Let 𝒱 be
   334	the set of all values G_i(P)/ℓ over all (i, ℓ, P). Then |𝒱| ≤ Φπ_JW.
   335	
   336	**Prop RB.** (i) γ_𝔇(𝒮_B ∖ 𝒱) = 0.
   337	(ii) Every input of the form "#(𝒮 ∩ I) is bounded above by …" (DS-U, L2_fam, Rankin, Brun–Titchmarsh-type) holds for
   338	𝒮′ := 𝒮_B ∖ 𝒱 because 𝒮′ ⊂ 𝒮_B.
   339	(iii) Every input of the form "Σ_{I∈ℐ}|#(𝒮 ∩ I) − main(I)| ≤ err" (HT local estimates, Lemma U1, Lemma 8.5′(R′),
